    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d852">

                <pb facs="1086" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg1074"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">892.014/8–2246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Siam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stanton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-30T18:00:00-04:00">August 30, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>720. Conditions appear dangerously explosive and imperative fuller reporting
                    conditions Battambang and border areas Siamese side. Suggest Mil Attaché,
                    Thompson or Bulkley<anchor n="78" xml:id="d852-f1"/> proceed Battambang and keep
                    area covered as fully as possible. Actual presence and continuing observation
                    may also have similar successful restraining influence Law<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d852-f2"/> visit Laos border May–June. Essential US have reports own
                    observers.</p>
                <p>Include in each important urtel (Deptel 687, Aug 15<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d852-f3"/>) request that Dept repeat Paris and London (urtel 973,
                    Aug 22).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d852-f1" n="78" xml:id="d852-f1-content">
                <p>Dwight H. Bulkley, Vice Consul at Bangkok.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d852-f2" n="79" xml:id="d852-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. William Law, Assistant Military Attaché in Siam.</p>
